# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Job Hunter - ignore rules
#
# Four lifecycle classes live in this repo:
#   INPUT      resumes/  profiles/     (yours, may contain PII - never commit)
#   OUTPUT     reports/                (generated - never commit)
#   TOOLING    .agents/ .opencode/ tools/
#   SCAFFOLD   templates/ config/ docs/
#
# Everything under INPUT and OUTPUT is ignored wholesale. The PII-free
# starting points a new user needs live in templates/ and config/.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Dependencies -----------------------------------------------------------
node_modules/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/

# Lockfiles ARE committed (see the negations at the bottom) so a fresh clone
# installs byte-identical portal dependencies via `bun install --frozen-lockfile`.

# --- USER INPUT (PII) --------------------------------------------------------
# Every resume the user supplies, in any format, plus the extracted-text cache.
# The directory itself is NOT excluded (only its contents), so the tracked
# resumes/README.md can be re-included below - git cannot re-include a file
# whose parent directory is excluded.
/resumes/*
!/resumes/README.md
# The generated profile, the per-persona YAML, the user's editable inputs and
# all per-profile job state. The directory itself is NOT excluded (only its
# contents), so the tracked profiles/README.md can be re-included below - git
# cannot re-include a file whose parent directory is excluded. A fresh clone
# therefore has the directory, and the documented first step works.
/profiles/*
!/profiles/README.md

# --- GENERATED OUTPUT --------------------------------------------------------
/reports/
/tmp_searches/
/salary_data.json

# --- PER-PROFILE STATE -------------------------------------------------------
# Belt-and-braces: the two rules above already cover profiles/, but state files
# are also ignored by name so a future layout change cannot leak them.
**/state/seen_jobs.json
**/state/tracker.csv
**/state/search-queries.md
**/state/scratch/
**/company_research/*.json

# --- Secrets -----------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# --- Binary / personal media -------------------------------------------------
# Resumes are commonly PDF or DOCX; the DOCX case is covered by /resumes/ but
# the pattern stays for safety.
*.pdf
*.docx
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.png

# --- OS / editor -------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.Zone.Identifier
.vscode/
.idea/

# --- Claude Code leftovers ----------------------------------------------------
.claude/projects/
.claude/settings.local.json

# --- Legacy layout (pre-migration) --------------------------------------------
# These paths only exist until the P1 restructure completes; the rules are
# removed in that same change. They exist now so the baseline commit can never
# capture PII from the old layout.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# MUST be committed - explicit negations so a future broad rule cannot hide
# the parts of the project other people need.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
!.agents/
!.agents/skills/
!.agents/skills/*/SKILL.md
!.agents/skills/*/url-reference.md
!.agents/skills/*/cli/
!.agents/skills/*/cli/src/
!.agents/skills/*/cli/tests/
!.agents/skills/*/cli/package.json
!.agents/skills/*/cli/tsconfig.json
!.agents/skills/*/cli/README.md

!.opencode/
!.opencode/commands/
!.opencode/agents/
!.opencode/skill/

!tools/
!templates/
!config/
!docs/
!resumes/README.md
!profiles/README.md

# The workspace lockfile is committed so a fresh clone installs byte-identical
# dependencies with `bun install --frozen-lockfile`.
!bun.lock
